Z||000000||BellaFiero||07-19-2000||11:58 AM||||Well, I've used it twice now, and it works quite well. The driver side motor keeps going out - it won't raise the light unless I manually get up and open the headlight door on the hood. I've pulled the motor, opened 'er up, and peered inside. THe large white gear ( this is for an '88 mind you ) is chewed to bits. So I filled the danged compartment with BONDO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> And it's worked for about a year. But now it's going out again. It's a quick fix, but not a permanent one, I guess. Still, it lasted a year... Now, I don't know whether to replace the gear or to fill it up with Bondo yet again... how many times will that work before the whole thing is chewed to smithereens? Does anyone have the gears for the '88 motors? I tried Rodney Dickman's rebuild kit for the 88's and I got three small plastic bits... uhm... ????? HUH?||||reg||3
Z||000001||Seanh||07-19-2000||02:58 PM||||Check out the Fiero Store. I got mine for the 86 motors and rebuilt them. It was all they needed. They are kinda high I think, but check them out:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-19-2000||03:45 PM||||87 and 88 Fieros use a different drive system then the earlier models. The three "round things" fit into the housing and act as clutches (?). Along with the round things, you should have received instructions from Rodney. I did when I bought mine. If not, send him an e-mail and I'd be willing to bet he would send them to you.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
